2. vggt and Depth-Anything-V2

   CoWTracker imports these two projects as git submodules, and `server/bootstrap.sh`
   fetches them with it:
   - vggt, https://github.com/facebookresearch/vggt
   - Depth-Anything-V2, https://github.com/DepthAnything/Depth-Anything-V2
   Their licences are not recorded in this repository. Check them upstream.
   Their terms apply to the copies that bootstrap.sh installs.

3. Other dependencies

   fabric-stretch depends on open source libraries (Rust crates such as egui/eframe,
   wgpu, serde, and Python packages numpy, opencv-python-headless, Pillow and pyserial).
   Cargo and pip install them under their own licences. Release binaries include their
   notices in licenses/: rust.html for Rust crates, python/ for Python, Tcl/Tk and
   bundled Python packages. The PyInstaller bootloader uses its upstream licence
   exception for distributing frozen applications.
   The pyueye Python bindings are included under their upstream terms. The IDS uEye
   driver and camera SDK libraries must be installed separately and are not bundled.

4. Measurement data

